## Conclusion

In this experiment, we created a C program that accepts memory size in megabytes as a command-line argument and dynamically allocates the requested memory using `malloc()`. We used `memset()` to access the allocated memory and the Linux `free` command to observe changes in memory usage. This experiment helped us understand dynamic memory allocation and memory monitoring in Linux
